WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

light-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Galaxies sit inside gas too faint to see

dip-1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Each gas cell leaves a shadow

dip-2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Moving gas shifts its shadow, like a siren

dip-3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Amount sets how much light is taken

dip-4
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Heat spreads it out

speed-1
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Where a dip sits tells its speed

speed-2
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Far apart, same speed, same dip

sum-1
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Dozens of shadows merge into a few dips

sum-2
00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Motion, not heat, makes this width

saturation-1
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
More gas, deeper dip

saturation-2
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Once black, only wider

lsf-1
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:28.000
A blurry telescope merges dips

lsf-2
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Blur turns black dips grey

noise-1
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:45.000
Longer exposures beat the noise

noise-2
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Noise can hide dips, and invent them

fit-1
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:57.000
We fit a few clouds

fit-2
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:03.000
The total O VI survives

fit-3
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:10.000
The clouds are not the cells

yourturn-1
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Now it is yours. Same galaxy, same beam
